  "notes": "USAGE:\nA hybrid word combining the kanji {凡|ぼん} (ordinary, mediocre) with the English loanword ミス (miss/mistake). Very common in school, sports, and work contexts. Often used self-critically.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {凡|ぼん}ミスをする: to make a careless mistake\n- {凡|ぼん}ミスを{減|へ}らす: to reduce careless mistakes\n- {凡|ぼん}ミスが{目立|めだ}つ: careless mistakes stand out\n- {凡|ぼん}ミスを{連発|れんぱつ}する: to make careless mistakes in succession",
